#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1020.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093292} :activity/id #uuid "a24a9109-b7af-5350-aa19-333930689bdd" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050106 :topic/id #uuid "2dc6eb82-3916-5e64-afe7-d715d1616fab" :topic/math-academy-id 919} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093292 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093390 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to find all of the solutions to\n\n![](images/4a/4ad61501c6c9b94fa05be806aead4f481a1e1e2f1f34b8cfb346ce685424b1f9.svg)\n\nNotice that this equation contains a transformed sine function. \n\nRecall that the general solution of the elementary equation $\\sin{X} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi , & \\, & \\, & X & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi ,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is assumed to be any integer.\n\nTo find the general solution of the transformed sine equation, we replace $X$ with the sine function's input, which is $x-\\dfrac{\\pi}3$ in this case. This gives the general solution\n\n$$\nx - \\dfrac{\\pi}3 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} + 2n\\pi, \\qquad\\qquad x - \\dfrac{\\pi}3 = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{3} + 2n\\pi.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above two equations for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi  & \\, & \\, & x & =\\pi +2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+\\frac{6n\\pi }{3} & \\, & \\, & x & =(1+2n)\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{2\\pi (1+3n)}{3} & \\, & \\, &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $n=0,\\pm1,\\pm2,\\ldots$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\leq x <2\\pi.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\dfrac{2\\pi}3$ and $x=\\pi.$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\leq x < 2\\pi.$ So, the solutions $x_1$ and $x_2$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx_1 = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{3},\\qquad x_2 = \\pi.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "1d59e641-96b3-527c-98e2-41c5def454e8" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2683 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "2352b7c0-f2bc-5425-8e29-fee849b6de7e" :step/math-academy-id 472590 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093293}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093293 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092363 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092001 :question/id #uuid "6b5d0a58-966a-5013-9cc3-4e43cadc561b" :question/math-academy-id "e-3821"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "78b2a447-e4fb-563a-9449-f8cc93e879e4" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049936}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092518} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092776} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092833} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542128} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542148} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542201} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542223}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Sine Function Transformed by One Operation"} :step/id #uuid "a71501a9-7f9a-5d4e-be8d-4b9e777ba08c" :step/math-academy-id 472591 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093294}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093294 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092364 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091992 :question/id #uuid "fc247d01-adf4-5c15-82dc-b6a209310d79" :question/math-academy-id "e-3776"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ef2dca3-f0f4-5bd9-8970-089b80acfad4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092630} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092836} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542156} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542195} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542200} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542204}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Containing the Sine Function Transformed by Multiple Operations"} :step/id #uuid "af8223f7-45e3-5db6-b8fe-5f8a0743ff84" :step/math-academy-id 472595 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093295}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186093295 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092365 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186091996 :question/id #uuid "7bc0e3e8-365a-5c32-99e4-2de6824fbcff" :question/math-academy-id "e-3790"}